servings: 4 servings
time required: 1 hour
alternative_name: Crustless Egg and Cheese Quiche
ingredient_count: 12
---

  Heat oven to 325 degrees with the rack positioned at the top. Butter a deep 8-inch round, square or oval #casserole{} generously with @unsalted butter{for greasing} and sprinkle all over with @fine plain dry bread crumbs{1%tablespoons}.

Heat the @unsalted butter{2%tablespoons} in a large pan over medium-high heat. When melted and foamy, add the @wild or button mushrooms{2 heaping cups}(stemmed and thinly sliced) and cook until lightly browned, about ~{3-5%minutes}. Scatter the cooked mushrooms and @grated cheese{1%cup}(such as Comté, Gruyère, Emmental or Cheddar) over the bread crumbs.

Whisk together the @half-and-half or heavy cream{1%cup}, @whole milk{1%cup}, @eggs{4}(lightly beaten), @kosher salt{1/2%teaspoon}, @freshly ground black pepper{1/2%teaspoon} and @freshly grated nutmeg{1/2%teaspoon}. Pour the mixture over the cheese. Sprinkle the top with @freshly grated Parmesan{1/4%cup}, and bake until the top is golden and the custard is just set in the center, about ~{40-45%minutes}. Set aside ~{5-10%minutes} to cool before serving. Sprinkle with @chives{2%tablespoons}(finely chopped), cut into wedges or scoop out, and serve.